WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.744
After seeing the freshly painted fence, Aunt Polly decided to let Tom play outdoors for the rest of the afternoon.

2
00:00:06.745 --> 00:00:12.546
The first thing Tom wanted to do was get revenge on Sid for telling Aunt Polly about his collar.

3
00:00:12.547 --> 00:00:18.182
So Tom waited by the fence and ambushed his half brother with balls made of dried-up mud.

4
00:00:18.183 --> 00:00:23.941
Before Aunt Polly could rush to Sid's rescue, Tom managed to hit him with six or seven balls.

5
00:00:23.942 --> 00:00:31.247
Sid screamed in fear and pain. Then Tom jumped over the fence and was

6
00:00:31.248 --> 00:00:38.557
gone. When Tom arrived at the town square a few minutes later, a group of boys was already there, ready to play army

7
00:00:38.558 --> 00:00:46.493
games. Tom and his best friend, Joe Harper, were appointed as generals, and they commanded their armies all

8
00:00:46.494 --> 00:00:54.213
afternoon. As the sun began to set, the boys counted their "dead" and "wounded," and it was determined that Tom had won a great

9
00:00:54.214 --> 00:00:58.891
battle. Joe and Tom shook hands and agreed to meet next Saturday for another

10
00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:02.430
battle. On his way home, Tom spied a new

11
00:01:02.431 --> 00:01:08.141
girl. He thought the new girl was lovely, with blue eyes and braided blond

12
00:01:08.142 --> 00:01:14.176
hair. At the sight of this new angel, the love Tom had pledged to a girl named Amy Lawrence instantly

13
00:01:14.177 --> 00:01:17.314
vanished. Tom soon began to show off for the new

14
00:01:17.315 --> 00:01:23.706
girl. He balanced a stick on his nose, and he walked up and down the street where they both

15
00:01:23.707 --> 00:01:28.586
lived. When the girl reached her house, she halted and looked over at Tom for only a

16
00:01:28.587 --> 00:01:30.880
second. But it was enough to encourage

17
00:01:30.881 --> 00:01:36.337
Tom. After she went inside, Tom lingered near her house, hoping to see her one more

18
00:01:36.338 --> 00:01:39.710
time. But the pretty new girl never

19
00:01:39.711 --> 00:01:43.701
reappeared. Still, Tom returned home in high

20
00:01:43.702 --> 00:01:48.300
spirits. His aunt scolded him for throwing mud balls at Sid, but Tom didn't

21
00:01:48.301 --> 00:01:52.766
care. When his aunt hit him for stealing sugar from the sugar bowl, Tom didn't

22
00:01:52.767 --> 00:01:57.706
care. He just smiled and said, "You never hit Sid when he takes

23
00:01:57.707 --> 00:02:02.670
sugar." "Sid doesn't torment me the way you do," she reminded him.

24
00:02:02.671 --> 00:02:06.391
That night Tom went to bed with the new girl on his mind.

25
00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:09.955
He was determined to devise a way to get her to notice him.

26
00:02:09.956 --> 00:02:14.422
The next morning Aunt Polly forced Tom to put on his Sunday suit for church.

27
00:02:14.423 --> 00:02:21.441
After a quick breakfast, she escorted Tom to church to make sure he attended Sunday school.

28
00:02:21.442 --> 00:02:28.379
The day's lesson consisted of memorizing five verses of the Bible, but Tom was having a problem concentrating.

29
00:02:28.380 --> 00:02:35.473
At last the lesson ended, and Tom and the other students had a fifteen-minute break before the church service began.

30
00:02:35.474 --> 00:02:43.208
Although Tom had not bothered to memorize the five verses, he had finally devised a plan to make the new girl interested in him.

31
00:02:43.209 --> 00:02:51.354
The other children had paid Tom to let them paint, so now his pockets overflowed with marbles, candies, fishhooks, and other goodies.

32
00:02:51.355 --> 00:02:57.256
Tom decided to use his new wealth to buy "verse recitation" tickets.

33
00:02:57.257 --> 00:03:01.958
These tickets were rewards for students who correctly recited verses from the Bible.

34
00:03:01.959 --> 00:03:06.806
For every two lines of verse correctly recited, students were given one blue ticket.

35
00:03:06.807 --> 00:03:12.256
Ten blue tickets equaled one red ticket; ten red tickets equaled one yellow ticket.

36
00:03:12.257 --> 00:03:15.833
For ten yellow tickets, a student could earn a Bible.

37
00:03:15.834 --> 00:03:19.725
A Bible for reciting two thousand lines of verse!

38
00:03:19.726 --> 00:03:25.096
Only older students were able to earn a Bible because it took years of saving tickets.

39
00:03:25.097 --> 00:03:28.994
Tom didn't want a Bible, but he did want to win the new girl's heart.

40
00:03:28.995 --> 00:03:33.977
To win her heart, he had decided that he must seem like a better person than the other boys.

41
00:03:33.978 --> 00:03:39.025
In church, the moment to impress the new girl finally came.

42
00:03:39.026 --> 00:03:43.748
First the minister asked all the smartest and most studious children how many tickets they had.

43
00:03:43.749 --> 00:03:46.418
None of them had enough for a Bible yet.

44
00:03:46.419 --> 00:03:50.824
"Does anyone have enough tickets for a Bible?" asked the minister.

45
00:03:50.825 --> 00:03:53.523
To the shock of everyone, Tom stood up.

46
00:03:53.524 --> 00:03:59.563
Then he proudly marched forward to bring his tickets to the minister.

